# Sitecore Development Patterns

## Component Registration

When creating Sitecore components:

- Export component from component file
- Use descriptive, PascalCase names
- Include TypeScript interfaces for props
- Handle missing fields gracefully

```typescript
// Example component
interface HeroProps {
  fields: {
    title: Field;
    subtitle: Field;
    backgroundImage: Field;
  };
}

export default function Hero({ fields }: HeroProps) {
  return (
    <div>
      <Text field={fields?.title} tag="h1" />
      <Text field={fields?.subtitle} tag="p" />
      <Image field={fields?.backgroundImage} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Content Management

Field Handling:

- Always check field existence: `fields?.title`
- Use Sitecore field components: `<Text field={} />`, `<RichText field={} />`
- Provide fallback content for missing fields
- Validate field data when necessary

Layout Service:

- Use layout service for page data
- Handle layout service errors gracefully
- Implement proper loading states
- Cache layout responses appropriately

## Configuration

Environment Setup:

- Use `.env.local` for local development
- Never commit API keys to version control
- Use `.env.example` to document required variables
- Configure Sitecore endpoints in `sitecore.config.ts`

Security:

- Validate all content from Sitecore
- Sanitize user inputs
- Use HTTPS for all Sitecore connections
- Implement proper error boundaries

